\f0\b \cf0 Files/Folders in Dataset and Description of Files \
(For zip, tar, or other packaged files, include file/folder structure within the packaged file)\
\pard\tx360\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b0 \cf0 1.	[data-processing-overview.pdf] - This file is a PDF that covers the organization of the workflow for the VT-Natural-Motion-Processing code repository, how the data flows through the files and how the files are used to train and evaluate models. The code allows for motion inference with a sparse set of inertial sensors, as well as visualizing the human motion in the dataset. This file shows which processing steps correspond to the different tutorials in dataset-tutorials.zip.\
2.	[dataset-tutorials.zip] - This file contains several tutorials for how to process the .mvnx or .h5 data files and interact with the dataset using the VT-Natural-Motion-Processing code repository (processing-code.zip and on GitHub).  The tutorials are both in Python (.ipynb extensions, which are Jupyter Notebooks for training deep learning models using the code repository) and PDF files (.pdf extensions, to be read easily with common PDF software). An overview of these tutorials is in the data-processing-overview.pdf file. The files include:\
\pard\tx1080\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl1\cf0 a.	01-dataset-tutorial.ipynb, 01-dataset-tutorial.pdf -- these files contain two sections. The first shows how to read in a small dataset and the second shows how to visualize full-body human motion. \
b.	02-deep-learning-tutorial.ipynb, 02-deep-learning-tutorial.pdf -- These files contain three sections. The sections (1) build a dataset, (2) train a neural network, and (3) test the neural network. \
c.	03-inference-tutorial.ipynb, 03-inference-tutorial.pdf -- Each file contains multiple sections including reading in data; loading a model; writing an inference function; running inference with the model, function, and data; and visualizing the results.\
\pard\tx360\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 3.	[dataset-metadata.xlsx] - The dataset metadata including the descriptions of the human motion and activities available in the .h5 and .mvnx files and the physical measurements taken of the participants during data collection sessions. The Excel file contains two sheets. The first sheet contains descriptions of the activities contained in the files. The second sheet contains the physical measurements of the participants taken before data collection, which are needed for the XSens engine.\
4.	[processing-code.zip] - This file is a zip file of all of the code used for processing of the dataset and machine learning with the dataset.  The code can convert the data from .mvnx format to .h5 format, train deep learning models of motion inference using PyTorch, perform motion inference using a sparse set of sensors, and visualize the results.  The most up-to-date code is located at https://github.com/ARLab-VT/VT-Natural-Motion-Processing. This file contains an MIT license.\
5.	[compressed_h5_dataset*.zip files] - The .h5 files contain human motion data for use with Python that were exported from .mvnx file format. These 25 files with .zip extension were in a compressed-h5-dataset folder. To use these files you will likely need to create this folder and rename the files to remove the \'91compressed_h5_dataset\'92 prefix.\
	The total compressed size is 297 Gb which becomes 390 Gb when uncompressed. Each .zip is approximately 12 Gb. Refer to the <Participant #>_<Day_#>_<Session #>.h5 description below for content within each .zip file. compressed-h5-dataset/ (parent directory) \
